WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:08.744
"Come and get it!"

2
00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:15.888
called Cookie.

3
00:00:17.128 --> 00:00:20.310
Frank and the other cowboys came up to Cookie's wagon.

4
00:00:22.271 --> 00:00:28.114
The children served the hungry men and everyone sat around a big fire to eat.

5
00:00:28.134 --> 00:00:33.341
"Frank says you can stay," Cookie said to Vinnie and Mandy.

6
00:00:33.361 --> 00:00:36.644
"But you'd better keep out of trouble."

7
00:00:36.664 --> 00:00:39.226
"We promise!"

8
00:00:39.926 --> 00:00:41.147
exclaimed the children.

9
00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:50.353
Mandy listened to the cowboys tell stories, and said, "I wish I had a cowboy hat and boots."

10
00:00:52.055 --> 00:00:53.716
"I wish I had a gun!"

11
00:00:54.356 --> 00:00:55.097
Vinnie cried.

12
00:00:55.117 --> 00:00:59.220
"Hey, kids," a cowboy called out.

13
00:01:00.692 --> 00:01:02.213
He held up a harmonica.

14
00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:04.695
"Sing something."

15
00:01:04.715 --> 00:01:09.319
"I can't sing," said Vinnie shyly.

16
00:01:09.339 --> 00:01:11.040
"He's right!

17
00:01:11.521 --> 00:01:12.602
He can't sing!"

18
00:01:14.143 --> 00:01:15.004
giggled Mandy.

19
00:01:15.024 --> 00:01:18.606
"Come on," the cowboy said.

20
00:01:18.626 --> 00:01:22.650
"Singing calms the cattle, so they can sleep."

21
00:01:24.091 --> 00:01:25.332
"Like a lullaby?"

22
00:01:25.872 --> 00:01:26.513
asked Vinnie.

23
00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:34.318
"Yep. We all sing, so don't be shy," said the cowboy, and he began to play.

24
00:01:34.338 --> 00:01:46.066
"Oh, give me a home where the buffalo roam," sang Vinnie as the cattle mooed happily.

25
00:01:47.087 --> 00:01:50.209
Meanwhile, Mandy was helping Cookie clean up.

26
00:01:50.229 --> 00:01:53.232
"What is the Chisholm Trail?"

27
00:01:53.772 --> 00:01:54.312
she asked.

28
00:01:54.332 --> 00:01:59.156
"Well, we take the cattle from Texas along the trail to Kansas.

29
00:02:00.576 --> 00:02:05.599
The cattle end up at the market where they are sold," explained Cookie.

30
00:02:05.619 --> 00:02:08.220
"How long does it take?"

31
00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:09.621
asked Mandy.

32
00:02:09.641 --> 00:02:13.944
"Depends on the weather and the Indians," said Cookie.

33
00:02:13.964 --> 00:02:17.085
"It can take from two to three months."

34
00:02:18.566 --> 00:02:23.489
Later some cowboys unrolled their beds and went to sleep.

35
00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:31.377
Others just leaned back, covered their eyes with their hats, and slept on the ground.

36
00:02:33.317 --> 00:02:35.698
Cookie gave Mandy and Vinnie bedrolls.

37
00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:37.139
Vinnie yawned.

38
00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:41.941
A few men were walking around, staring at the herd.

39
00:02:43.622 --> 00:02:45.302
"Why aren't those men sleeping?"

40
00:02:45.883 --> 00:02:46.963
Vinnie asked Frank.

41
00:02:46.983 --> 00:02:50.905
"They're guarding the cattle," Frank replied.

42
00:02:50.925 --> 00:02:53.226
"From what?"

43
00:02:53.746 --> 00:02:54.466
asked Mandy.

44
00:02:54.486 --> 00:03:00.025
"Wild animals, cattle thieves, and Indians," said Frank.

45
00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:03.588
The children heard howling in the distance.

46
00:03:04.829 --> 00:03:07.031
Mandy moved closer to her brother.

47
00:03:08.272 --> 00:03:12.455
The next morning, the children woke to a sunny day.

48
00:03:13.656 --> 00:03:16.138
Everyone was already up and ready to go.

49
00:03:17.479 --> 00:03:22.083
The wagon was loaded, and the cattle were starting to move again.

50
00:03:22.103 --> 00:03:25.906
"Good morning, kids," Cookie called.

51
00:03:25.926 --> 00:03:30.889
"You missed breakfast, but I saved you some biscuits.

52
00:03:32.189 --> 00:03:33.070
We have to get going."

53
00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:37.592
"Where?" asked Vinnie, munching on his biscuit.

54
00:03:38.812 --> 00:03:44.935
"It's time to get back on the trail," said Frank as he brought over Vinnie's horse from the

55
00:03:44.975 --> 00:03:45.875
previous day.

56
00:03:47.076 --> 00:03:48.977
The horse sniffed Vinnie's biscuit.

57
00:03:48.997 --> 00:03:50.997
"You come with me."

58
00:03:51.018 --> 00:03:56.540
"And Mandy can ride with me," said Cookie.

59
00:03:57.676 --> 00:04:00.838
He picked her up and helped her climb onto the wagon seat.

60
00:04:02.199 --> 00:04:05.021
The horses followed the cattle at an easy pace.

61
00:04:06.362 --> 00:04:09.584
They rode over dry, flat prairies of tall grass.

62
00:04:11.005 --> 00:04:14.588
The sun was hot, and the sky was bright blue.

63
00:04:15.929 --> 00:04:17.250
There was a soft wind.

64
00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:25.576
Vinnie wiped his face with his sleeve and thought: "This is the life of a cowboy!"
